<title>UK: MOTOR RACING-TYRRELL NOT CONCERNED BY VERSTAPPEN'S ABSENCE FROM.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-TYRRELL NOT CONCERNED BY VERSTAPPEN'S ABSENCE FROM.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tyrrell made it clear on Monday</p>
<p>there were no problems with their new signing Dutchman Jos</p>
<p>Verstappen despite his absence from the official entry list for</p>
<p>next year's Formula One world championship.</p>
<p>&quot;We  think the problem was just down to  timing,&quot;</p>
<p>explained team spokesman Rupert Manwaring.</p>
<p>&quot;We signed Jos late  on  Thursday night and he  will</p>
<p>definitely be our driver next year. His absence may just be</p>
<p>because the list was put together before we announced him.&quot;</p>
<p>There  were  no  surprises  in  the  24-strong  list,</p>
<p>released in Paris by the International Automobile Federation</p>
<p>(FIA), which confirmed vacant seats at the Jordan, Ligier,</p>
<p>Minardi and Lola teams.</p>
<p>The  four teams have until March 9, the day  before</p>
<p>practice begins for the Australian Grand Prix, to nominate their</p>
<p>drivers.</p>
<p>	  Entry list:</p>
<p> 1. Damon Hill (Britain)		- Arrows</p>
<p> 2. Pedro Diniz (Brazil)		- Arrows</p>
<p> 3. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)     - Williams</p>
<p> 4. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) - Williams</p>
<p> 5. Michael Schumacher (Germany)    - Ferrari</p>
<p> 6. Eddie Irvine (Britain)	    - Ferrari</p>
<p> 7. Jean Alesi (France)		 - Benetton</p>
<p> 8. Gerhard Berger (Austria)	  - Benetton</p>
<p> 9. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   - McLaren</p>
<p> 10. David Coulthard (Britain)	- McLaren</p>
<p> 11. Ralf Schumacher (Germany)	- Jordan</p>
<p> 12. To be announced		    - Jordan</p>
<p> 14. Olivier Panis (France)	   - Ligier</p>
<p> 15. TBA				    - Ligier</p>
<p> 16. Johnny Herbert (Britain)	 - Sauber</p>
<p> 17. Nicola Larini (Italy)	    - Sauber</p>
<p> 18. TBA				    - Tyrrell</p>
<p> 19. Mika Salo (Finland)		- Tyrrell</p>
<p> 20. TBA				    - Minardi</p>
<p> 21. TBA				    - Minardi</p>
<p> 22. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)    - Stewart</p>
<p> 23. Jan Magnussen (Denmark)	  - Stewart</p>
<p> 24. TBA				    - Lola</p>
<p> 25. TBA				    - Lola</p>
